ift.", "watch": "Any credible polling showing Macy within single digits, or major outside spending entering on her behalf, would warrant moving this toward the Tossup range.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Incumbent Ben Cline (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Ben Cline seeks another term in a Shenandoah Valley–anchored district that leans about twelve points Republican, giving the incumbent a strong structural advantage. He has been renominated without difficulty and faces no outside spending against him, while prediction markets give him roughly a 93% chance of holding the seat.\n\nDemocrat Beth Macy, a former Roanoke Times journalist, has run a competitive financial operation, outraising Cline and entering the fall with more cash on hand. That money gives her a path to make the race competitive on the airwaves, but with no public polling and no expert ratings flagging the district as contested, the fundamentals still point firmly toward Cline in a district this red.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0375, "margin": -14.4}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0454, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0463, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0654, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0527, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0505, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0614, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0306, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0328, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0472, "margin": -13.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0358, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.036, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0359, "margin": -14.0}]}